| 9 | Poisson Distribution with example | ✅ |
| 10 | Z-score Probability | ✅ |
| 11 | PDF vs CDF | ✅ |

---

### Part B — Data Analysis & Testing Tasks

| # | Task | Distribution | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Fit Bernoulli & Binomial | Bernoulli / Binomial | p = 0.4455; Binomial mean ≈ 4.05/week |
| 2 | Fit Poisson distribution | Poisson | λ = 7.10 transactions/day |
| 3 | Model transaction amounts | Log-Normal + Power Law | Log-Normal: μ=8.00, σ=0.47 |
| 4 | Q-Q Plot for normality | Normal (test) | Raw amounts NOT normal; log-transform is near-normal |
| 5 | Box-Cox Transformation | Power transform | λ = −0.18; skewness reduced significantly |
| 6 | Z-Score & P(Amount > ₹5000) | Normal (Z) | 11.4% of transactions exceed ₹5000 |
| 7 | PDF & CDF of amounts | Empirical + Log-Normal | 88.6% of transactions ≤ ₹5000 |
| 8 | Best distribution fit | Comparison (KS Test) | **Log-Normal** is the best fit ✅ |

